# FTMO Risk & Execution

## Risk guard (6 checks — do not bypass)

1. Daily loss limit (5% of SOD balance)
2. Max overall drawdown (10%)
3. Daily budget remaining > trade risk
4. Drawdown buffer remaining > trade risk
5. Max open positions (default: 1)
6. News blackout (±2 min HIGH-impact, leverage > 1:30)

## Order building

- `build_order()` returning `None` → **block trade**, log + alert — no fallback defaults
- Spread filter: block if spread > 10% of ATR
- Fixed dollar risk via tick_size / tick_value from MT5 — never guess
- Structure-aware SL: `MAX(ATR distance, structure distance)`
- Duplicate prevention: `oms.has_open_position()` before submit

## Execution

- Live orders only via `mt5.order_send()` in `core/execution.py`
- MT5 rejections → mark OMS REJECTED, log, Telegram alert
- `engine.run_pipeline_tick()` must return block_reason / risk_warnings for notifier

## Before changing this code

Ask user to confirm if change affects live trading behavior. Prefer demo test: `python main.py --tick-now`.
